/* ScamSense: Inbox Defender — AUTHORED case files (never generated live). All people, numbers and sites are fictional.
 *
 * HOW A CASE WORKS
 *  - A case is ONE organised operation (a "ring") plus real contacts who happen to be part of the same story.
 *    The ring hands you from member to member, reuses details, and plants small inconsistencies you can catch.
 *  - Nothing is multiple choice. The player TYPES. The text is classified into an INTENT (what are you trying to do?)
 *    by the real LLM when available (regex fallback offline). Replies are AUTHORED; the AI never writes scam dialogue.
 *  - Each chat has a style (STYLES) giving default replies/tells; a chat overrides only what makes it unique.
 *
 * SCRIPT STEPS:  "text" (them) · {w:ms} · {sys:"..."} · {go:"chatId"} (new contact starts) · {open:{...}} (free typing)
 * OPEN SPEC:  budget, vars (fill {placeholders}), replies {intent:[string | {m, fact:[k,v], go:id}]},
 *             tells {intent:label|null}, clears {intent:label}, loss {comply_*:{money,life,say}},
 *             events {afterNthQuestion:[messages, {go:id}]}, fallback [..], ultimatum [..]
 */
